e + N2(X) -> e + N2(C_3Pi_u). Su et al. J. Phys. B 54, 115203 (2021) (CC BY 4.0) below 20 eV; Johnson et al. J. Geophys. Res. 110, A11311 (2005) Table 2 from 20 eV; power-law continuation p = 2.47 above Johnson's last point (to 10 keV). Overlap Su/Johnson: 12.5 eV 3.09 (+-0.22), 15 eV 0.94 (+-0.18), 17.5 eV 2.25 (+-0.18), 20 eV 2.13 (+-0.18); step at 20 eV Su/Johnson = 2.13. Continuation share of the rate: T_e 20 eV 0.2 % (zero/hold tail -0.2/+0.1 %), T_e 30 eV 1.0 % (zero/hold tail -1.0/+0.8 %). Header 11.19 eV = experimental vertical excitation energy (Oddershede, Su 2021 Table 1); no threshold shift. Maxwellian-integrated by abep_sim/rate_tables.py (scripts/build_n2_electronic_excitation_tables.py). Reaction set abep-n2n-0.9.
